      <div class="faq">
        <h3>Questions leaders often ask</h3>
        <details><summary>Should GTM wait until the product is finished?</summary><p>No. Customer discovery, market research, positioning and pricing should inform development from the beginning. Commercial launch and scale should follow validation and operational readiness.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the difference between a POC and POR?</summary><p>A POC (Proof of Concept) tests feasibility and key assumptions. POR (Pilot, Optimise, Rollout) tests the solution in a real operating environment, improves it using evidence and establishes whether it can be scaled.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why does brand positioning matter for an AI product?</summary><p>It gives the market a clear reason to understand, trust and choose the company and its solution. Technical capability alone does not create differentiation or customer confidence.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What should leadership measure?</summary><p>Measures should connect the full journey: problem value, readiness, feasibility, operational performance, adoption, customer traction, pipeline, conversion, revenue and return on investment.</p></details>
